    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d241">

                <pb facs="0341" n="239" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Advisory Committee/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland (Wilson), at
                        Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-16T20:00:00-05:00">March 16, 1933—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>89. Department’s telegrams 85, March 11, 7 p.m., and 86, March 11, 8 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="68" xml:id="d241-f1"/> and your telegram 150, March 15, 8 p.m.</p>
                <p>For guidance:</p>
                <p>The Department desires that you do not participate in conversations which may
                    take place in connection with the examination of “problems of the export of arms
                    in relation to the present situation in the Far East” other than, if asked, to
                    state the attitude and policy of this Government as set forth in the pertinent
                    sections of Department’s 85, March 11, 7 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
